<title>CANADA: Suzy Shier Q2 loss turns to profit on gain.</title>
<headline>Suzy Shier Q2 loss turns to profit on gain.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			    1995</p>
<p> Shr   Profit	    C$3.15     Loss	 $0.18</p>
<p> Net   Profit	    40,300     Loss	 2,000</p>
<p> Revs		     110,000		   69,500</p>
<p>	   6 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr     Profit	  C$2.96     Loss	C$0.29</p>
<p> Net     Profit	  37,738     Loss	 3,385</p>
<p> Revs		     280,200		  130,100</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  12,761		   11,563</p>
<p>		(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note: Full company name is Suzy Shier Ltd. Latest quarter and six months includes C$39.6 million of non-recurring income less expenses from partial sale of investment and dilution of company's shares in U.K. subsidiary which completed a public offering on the A.I.M. of the London Stock Exchange on May 8. Sales in 1996 second quarter include C$38.2 million attributable to The Wet Seal Inc, whose results were consolidated with the company's up to May 24, 1996. From May 25, the company will account for its remaining share of Wet Seal earnings on an equity basis.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Montreal bureau (514) 985-2434</p>
